Bash

Bash (Bourne Again Shell) is the default command-line shell used in many Linux distributions.

A Bash Script is a text file containing multiple Linux commands that execute automatically.

Example Script
#!/bin/bash

echo "Hello World"

date

pwd
Save File
hello.sh
Make Executable
chmod +x hello.sh
Run Script
./hello.sh
Why Companies Use Bash Scripts
Automation
Daily backups
Log cleanup
User management
System monitoring
Maintenance tasks
